Feature: Laplace compiles witnessed substrate relations into neural target artifacts
  Laplace calculates model operators through its native vector ISA and PostgreSQL
  server engine. SQL orchestrates the computation. Source models provide attributable
  testimony, while target formats such as GGUF are exact compiled artifacts.

  Background:
    Given a package receipt identifying the loaded native engine and PostgreSQL extensions
    And a substrate containing witnessed precedence, containment, occurrence, syntax, semantic, context, provenance, and trust relations
    And a declared target architecture with every required tensor, layout, numeric, metadata, and quantization contract

  Scenario: A relation kernel becomes a query and key operator
    Given a declared pairwise kernel calculated from typed substrate relations
    And separate observations withheld from operator fitting
    When SQL submits the vector operator-fit and factorization program
    Then the native engine returns query and key factors with complete receipts
    And their bilinear scores match the declared kernel within its numeric bounds
    And the same bounds hold for the withheld observations
    And scalar and vector executions return the same values and dispositions

  Scenario: A generated AImap supplies target embedding coordinates
    Given a pinned typed operator over exact structure and selected epistemic layers generates an AImap whose dimension matches the declared target embedding width
    When selected vocabulary entities are projected into the target contract
    Then every embedding row traces to the AImap operator, evidence epoch, spectral recipe, domain row, and alignment receipt
    And a gauge rotation with compensated dependent operators preserves target behavior
    But treating the AImap as canonical physicality or permanent semantic authority fails layer separation

  Scenario: The prior direct attestation operator is independently reproduced
    Given witnessed relations for deterministic prompt entities and their neighbors
    When the engine constructs an identity embedding and attestation log-odds output operator
    And the target compiler emits a GGUF with the declared vocabulary and architecture
    Then an external runtime loads the GGUF and matrix multiplication exposes the witnessed relation signal
    And every completion is captured as behavioral evidence whether correct, noisy, or cyclic
    But this result does not count as evidence that query, key, value, or output projections carry the relation semantics

  Scenario: Heads implement different witnessed relation families
    Given separate target kernels for precedence, containment, syntax, semantic role, and causality
    When the engine constructs one declared head operator for each kernel
    Then every head best reproduces its declared relation family on withheld observations
    And every head receipt names the exact evidence, recipe, factorization, and output values
    But shuffling one relation family causes that head's mechanism test to fail

  @LP-TEST-MODEL-FLATTENING-REJECTION
  Scenario: A flattened representation cannot become the source of target intelligence
    Given precedence containment syntax semantic-role causality context provenance trust direction and time require distinct typed operators
    When one exporter replaces them with a universal adjacency matrix embedding similarity or scalar neighborhood
    Then at least one independently solved relation operator and withheld behavioral fixture must disagree
    And the exporter cannot recover the erased relation law evidence boundary direction or context from target shape
    But successful fitting on a small academic fixture cannot certify the missing target operations

  @LP-TEST-MODEL-ACCEPTANCE-INVARIANT-NAMED
  Scenario: Faithful is not an acceptance class
    Given an exported artifact has expected tensor shapes metadata and loadability
    When the exporter claims that the result is faithful
    Then the claim is rejected until it names exact preserved bytes layouts numeric bounds induced operators relation families evidence boundaries quantization error and runtime behaviors as applicable
    And each named invariant has an independent oracle withheld fixture and deliberate defect
    But resemblance correlation nonempty output or one successful runtime load cannot substitute for semantic and behavioral preservation

  Scenario: Gauge-equivalent factors compare through their induced operator
    Given query and key factors whose induced bilinear form is known
    And an invertible basis transform with its compensating inverse transform
    When the transform produces numerically different query and key factors
    Then the original and transformed factors produce the same bilinear form within the declared bound
    And they produce the same pairwise logits and target behavior on withheld probes
    And their factor content identities remain different
    And their induced operator equivalence receipt is the same
    But raw tensor distance is rejected as evidence of different semantics

  Scenario: Permuted heads and neurons retain functional equivalence
    Given a target block and a version with permuted heads and feed-forward neurons
    And every dependent projection is permuted consistently
    When both blocks execute the declared withheld probe set
    Then their induced functions and outputs agree within the declared numeric bound
    But an uncompensated permutation fails operator and behavior equivalence

  Scenario: Value and output operators reproduce contextual transformations
    Given witnessed input contexts, selected entities, and desired contextual results
    When SQL submits the vector value and output operator program
    Then the native result reproduces the declared contextual transformations within their bounds
    But a shape-compatible transposed or omitted factor fails the contextual behavior test

  Scenario: Source models are independent witnesses
    Given two unrelated source-model families and explicit substrate relations over shared content
    When their layers, heads, tensors, operators, activations, and behavior are decomposed
    Then every observation retains its model, architecture role, source, and value provenance
    And cross-model agreement and disagreement can be queried without selecting either model as authority
    And target construction can exclude either source model without changing substrate identity

  @LP-TEST-MODEL-BEHAVIOR-COORDINATE
  Scenario: Model behavior is admitted as a typed experiment rather than a floating probability
    Given a declared model architecture release layer head expert route context operation and candidate
    When the engine observes activation contribution downstream effect and a causal intervention under experiment E
    Then every observation retains the complete behavior coordinate and source-model provenance
    And behavior observed in another context or route remains a different witnessed occurrence
    But a token-pair probability without context operation experiment and effect cannot become a universal semantic relation

  @LP-TEST-MODEL-EFFECTIVE-SUPPORT @LP-TEST-MODEL-ARBITRARY-THRESHOLD-REJECTION
  Scenario: Measured effective support remains distinct from formal nonzero support
    Given a softmax or gated operator whose finite candidates all have formally nonzero support
    And withheld probes with causal ablation cumulative-mass contribution-norm and downstream-behavior measurements
    When a versioned effective-support recipe retains or prunes candidate contributions
    Then the receipt records the threshold law calibration boundary retained set discarded tail measured loss and behavioral equivalence bounds
    And top-k may accelerate candidate selection without becoming truth relevance or semantic authority
    But changing an arbitrary cutoff so a causally material candidate disappears must fail the withheld behavioral oracle

  Scenario: A complete target tensor set is emitted
    When the target compiler selects substrate state and constructs every declared tensor
    Then the declared, selected, calculated, factorized, emitted, quantized, loaded, and executed operator inventories match exactly
    And every output value traces to substrate state, ISA instructions, recipes, and numeric transformations
    But removing one required tensor or replacing it with a shape-compatible wrong value fails acceptance

  Scenario: GGUF is an exact target runtime artifact
    Given GGUF is the declared target container
    When the compiler emits the complete target artifact
    Then its tensor names, dimensions, layouts, architecture metadata, numeric conventions, and quantization match the target runtime
    And the real target runtime loads and executes the artifact
    And the artifact passes retrieval, reranking, attention, decoding, and conversation behavior required by its declared stage
    But a file that only parses, is nonempty, or has plausible dimensions does not pass

  Scenario: SQL executes model construction on CPU
    Given the package is running without an available GPU
    When SQL submits representative bulk relation-kernel, operator-fit, factorization, evaluation, quantization, and emission programs
    Then the loaded native PostgreSQL engine executes every stage on CPU
    And process, SPI, SQL, transaction, and allocation crossings are bounded by batch count rather than element count
    And the complete measurement reports input count, bytes, stages, throughput, latency, memory, writes, environment, artifacts, and receipts
